@startuml activity-narrative
' Asking Copilot for the narrative, and where "unverified" comes from.
' The forecast numbers are already saved before any of this starts.
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg 03-activity-narrative.puml

skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #2F6FB5
skinparam ArrowColor #5B6B7D

|#FDFAF3|You and the window|
start
if (AI narrative asked for?) then (no)
  :The run stays saved with ai_status = not_requested.
  You can ask for the words later from the Runs list;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

|#F6FAFF|Forecast service — still no AI numbers|
:Second HTTP call. Load the facts this run already saved;
:Start a Copilot session on the user's own signed-in
Copilot CLI. No key of any other provider;

repeat
  :Hand over the rule sheet ("never invent a number"),
  the facts, 8 read-only tools and 5 product skills;

  |#F2EDFA|GitHub Copilot — words only|
  :Call the read-only tools to look the numbers up;
  :Write one JSON document: run summary, per-member
  notes, team risks, suggested moves, model notes;

  |#F6FAFF|Forecast service — still no AI numbers|
  :Check the reply's shape against a strict template.
  An unexpected field, a missing section or an
  over-long paragraph fails;
repeat while (shape valid?) is (no — 2 attempts, then failed) not (yes)

:Pull every number out of the prose and look for it
among the facts that sentence is allowed to quote.
Whole numbers of 20 or less are ignored unless
they are written with an hours unit;

if (every number matched?) then (yes)
  #EAF6EF:ai_status = ok;
else (no)
  #FDF6E9:ai_status = unverified.
  The text is still saved and still shown,
  with an information banner above it;
endif

:Store the whole exchange — the exact facts sent, the
reply, the check report, the model and the timings —
and update the run's ai_status;

|#FDFAF3|You and the window|
:The AI Summary panel fills in on the Team result screen,
per-member notes appear on the Member screens, and the
Rebalancing page lists the suggested moves;
stop

note right
  If anything goes wrong the numbers are untouched —
  only ai_status records it:
  failed:not_signed_in · failed:cli_unavailable ·
  failed:timeout (no answer in 240 s) ·
  failed:model_error · failed:invalid_output ·
  failed:other
end note
@enduml
